# lab.scene: three spatially disjoint test blocks, each exercising one
# diff class. Blocks occupy separate screen thirds so none can occlude
# another; per-block provenance lives in labels/lab_labels.json.
# Camera looks down +z; light fixed so both renderers share shading.
fovx 60
light 1.5 2.0 0.5
ambient 0.15

# === occlusion block (left third) ===
# Two overlapping triangles with different depth slopes whose surfaces
# cross over a broad interior footprint. The depth-crossing line is placed
# by float32 perspective interpolation (raster) vs float64
# Moller-Trumbore (tracer). The winner flips across a wide 2D band whose
# pixels have no local id coexistence -> occlusion class, scaling ~ O(s^2).
tri -1.50 -0.90 3.90  -0.45 -0.90 4.10  -0.975 0.90 4.00000  0.85 0.30 0.15
tri -1.50 -0.90 4.10  -0.45 -0.90 3.90  -0.975 0.90 3.99999  0.20 0.45 0.85

# === boundary block (middle third) ===
# Two long triangles overlapping only in a thin vertical strip, with depth
# planes that cross inside that strip. Disputed pixels form a roughly
# one-pixel-wide line where both ids coexist locally -> boundary class,
# scaling ~ O(s). The narrow overlap keeps interior (occlusion-type)
# disagreement negligible.
tri -0.40 -0.90 3.00000   0.00 -0.90 3.00000   0.00 0.90 3.00000  0.90 0.75 0.20
tri  0.00 -0.90 3.00003   0.40 -0.90 3.00003  -0.02 0.90 2.99997  0.25 0.65 0.85

# === precision block (right third) ===
# One isolated flat triangle, no overlap and no shared edge. Both
# renderers emit the same primitive id on every covered pixel; the only
# residual delta is the float32 edge/interpolation path vs float64
# intersection -> precision class, scaling ~ O(s^2).
tri 0.45 -0.40 5.50  1.50 -0.40 5.50  0.975 0.45 5.50   0.55 0.55 0.55
